<title>JAPAN: Sanyo to launch PC with Intel MMX in March.</title>
<headline>Sanyo to launch PC with Intel MMX in March.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sanyo Electric Co Ltd said on Thursday that it would start selling on March 1 a notebook personal computer (PC) using Intel Corp's MMX Pentium processors.</p>
<p>The MMX Pentium chip, which was unveiled on Wednesday, is a new chip which supports various multimedia functions, including video and audio data processing.</p>
<p>Sanyo said in a statement it plans to sell its new PC Winkey for 620,000 yen.</p>
<p>Earlier on Thursday, Toshiba Corp said it had already started selling notebook and desktop computers using MMX Pentium chips.</p>
</text>
